post_remove() {
  cat <<'MSG'
==> Saya Studio removed. pacman never touches home directories, so these
    user-level files are left behind. Delete them yourself if you want them gone:

    Native messaging manifests written by the app at startup (respect $XDG_CONFIG_HOME):
      ~/.config/google-chrome/NativeMessagingHosts/com.saya.studio.json
      ~/.config/chromium/NativeMessagingHosts/com.saya.studio.json
      ~/.config/BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/NativeMessagingHosts/com.saya.studio.json
    (They point at /usr/share/saya-studio/saya_native_host.py, which no longer exists.)

    Also remove the browser extension from brave://extensions or chrome://extensions.

    Application data (database, backups, Civitai bridge token and jobs) is kept in:
      ~/.local/share/studio.saya.desktop   (or $XDG_DATA_HOME/studio.saya.desktop)
    Delete it only after making a backup; models, images and workflows are never removed.
MSG
}
